# Local dev config.
#
# Phase 2 (submissions + admin triage) is enabled here AND in .env.production —
# it ships. This file exists because the two builds still differ in one way that
# matters: locally there is no Turnstile site key and no Cognito pool, so
# SuggestButton renders the form anyway (import.meta.env.PROD is false) and
# AdminAuthProvider falls back to its sessionStorage token. That is what lets
# submissions.cy.ts and admin_triage.cy.ts run with no AWS account.
#
# Neither difference is a security boundary: the server independently requires a
# captcha whenever it is hosted (utilities/turnstile.py, fails closed) and
# refuses the dev admin token the moment a pool is configured (api/auth.py).
VITE_ENABLE_SUBMISSIONS=true
